      "message": "fix(post): Sodick Mark 21 header names its control and its threading\n\nThe Sodick wire post header now names the Mark 21 / EX21 control. It\nwarns LN1W / LN2W owners that G21 alarms (E00170) and the taper words\ndiffer, and it points them to the Sodick Wire EDM (LN2W) post. The post\ndescription says the same.\n\nThe threading line now matches the program. With AWT it reads\n\"PROGRAM THREADS THE WIRE WITH T91 AT START\". Without AWT it says the\noperator threads the wire at the M00.\n\nOnly comment lines and the description change. Every code line of the\neight goldens is byte-identical.\n\nFixes #4046\nFixes #4044\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
